WEBVTT

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.300
<b>This program is a work of fiction. The characters, organizations, locations, cases, etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.</b>

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:14.950
What's this?

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.530
Are you by yourself?

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.920
Don't bullshit me.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.130
Ryang-Ha Song...

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.450
Just who are you?

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.060
We're in danger of being attacked.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.770
We have to escape, quickly!

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.180
Come in.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.140
Donald Bachmann.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.900
We call him Donny.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.750
Welcome,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.660
Ryang-Ha Song.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.880
Why don't we have a chat?

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.160
This world always abandons the weak.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.860
Children of war-torn lands 
raised as child soldiers.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:53.470
Children of poverty, 
sold off by their own parents.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:57.930
Children doped up and 
forced into dealing drugs.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.560
Children born in prison, 
branded as criminals from birth.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.790
Their existence is erased in the shadows of 
society's injustices, unbeknownst to all.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:16.190
I take in such children and give them names.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.700
That's the case for everyone here.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.750
Are you trying to rope me 
into charity work or something?

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.740
Unfortunately, I'm not too interested.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.260
Oh, it's nothing out of the ordinary.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.170
I'll take this off now.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.140
There you go.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.790
Now, that was a lengthy introduction.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.440
Let's get to business.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.120
Nice to meet you, Ryang-Ha Song.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.570
This is our first time meeting,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.940
but your name is familiar to me.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:02.420
I believe it's one of the 
names I once gave.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.600
I believe it's one of the 
names I once gave.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.250
Huh?

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.840
Let's see...

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.240
Does that mean Mr. Song is our big brother?

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.740
Yay!

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.750
Hang on.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.640
What's going on here, Donny?

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.900
He's not just someone 
who has the same name?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.640
I never heard anything about this.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.360
It's as I told you, Nikka.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:03.610
Ryang-Ha Song was a member of my 
family, just like the rest of you.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.870
The one here is a phony, 
deliberately using his name.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.940
Hey, aren't you done with the garbage yet?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.420
Hurry it up!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.780
The ship's leaving soon!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.120
Hey, what kinda trash
 is that truck taking out?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.780
Oh, we were asked to transport it in secret.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.100
For fifty times the usual tip.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.980
Whoa, it better not be anything suspicious.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.350
I heard it's just green waste.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:38.610
The chef probably let some 
meat go bad or something.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.060
Huh, I see.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:49.990
Handing over Song, the threats to you, 
and his ambush are all connected, huh?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:54.210
He wanted me to deliver Ryang-Ha to Barosela.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:55.750
Which means...

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.580
There's a good chance they have a base there.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.000
Good thing we decided not to hand 
this guy over to the police.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.610
Depending on how big these guys are,

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.230
they might have the 
local police in their pocket.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:13.010
That would put us at a disadvantage.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.270
What do we do now, though, Chateau?

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:22.150
You aren't thinking about going 
to help Mr. Song, are you?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.620
Of course not.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.610
He's been a constant pain in my ass.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.160
I'm just really annoyed at him.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.780
You came up with some documents 
to build an identity for yourself

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.410
during your time at Santoukai, if I recall.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:41.090
Identification numbers 
for your country of origin,

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.640
in addition to residence records 
through the age of fifteen,

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.420
an academic history, medical history...

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:50.930
And all of it was identical 
to what I'd given Ryang-Ha.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:58.930
Now, who are you, and why do you 
call yourself Ryang-Ha Song?

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.320
Sheesh.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.630
I was expecting to meet someone 
a little more important.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.420
You're just a breeder.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:12.720
Dude...

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:16.830
And your training isn't even that great.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:22.310
Any kid can give their pet dog a name,

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.960
Mr. Supreme Commander.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:38.600
Nikka?

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:49.580
Damn it... Jinon, you prick.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:53.200
Who said you could kill him?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.580
Don't be a dumbass.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.080
Jinon...

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.580
Don't you dare.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.540
You're in the wrong.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.210
Stupid.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:04.710
Idiot.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.890
Doofus.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.000
Jeez, man.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.140
Everyone's getting hurt.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.410
It's already sunset.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.430
You must be tired after 
your long voyage, Jinon.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.930
Get some rest.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.660
Someone tried to reach you 
on this phone earlier.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.320
Was it one of your people?

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.930
Or perhaps your employer?

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:49.420
Either way, I'm sure we can get 
plenty of information with this.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.420
But I don't want to waste time on that.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.680
Where is Ryang-Ha Song?

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.680
You're bringing yourselves in, huh?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.560
That speeds things up a bit.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.780
They'll keep chasing you
 until I come home, anyway.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.480
You're better off giving yourselves up.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.570
That way, Donny won't hurt you.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:18.690
"Donny"?

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.820
Who is that?

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.830
Our boss.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.830
The owner of the underground 
armory in Barosela.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:35.080
The locals know him as 
the war starter—the Trigger.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:42.060
You see, Jinon,
 emotions are like water and oil.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.810
At times, they can strengthen a flame, 
and at others, they can snuff it out.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.570
Until I set things in motion, 
you children must remain pilot flames.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:57.000
And Mifa, no eating snacks in bed.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.790
Understood?

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:01.830
Hmm.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.550
Keep your strong emotions under control.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:09.080
For now, that is.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.700
So, where were you born?

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:13.750
How old?

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.980
You're up there, aren't you?

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.380
Like, thirty?

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.960
Maybe late twenties?

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.100
Nailed it, didn't I?

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:27.710
If you're going to interrogate me, 
do it when that Donny guy is around.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.100
It's a waste of time otherwise.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.750
I'm just shooting the breeze.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:35.980
This horrible wound I got protecting you 
is gonna take a whole week to heal.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.990
Why don't you be friends with me already?

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:42.210
Well, I'm half messing around,

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.120
but it's true that I'm kinda interested in you.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.630
About your time with the Santoukai.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.870
About what kind of hits you've carried out.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:59.560
And, honestly, about whether 
I could kill you in a one-on-one.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.250
Good thing Jinon did a shit job
 of checking you, huh?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.970
If it were me, I would've called you on that.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.570
Jim, can I ask you to do two things for me?

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:23.230
First, I want you to assign 
guards to my parents' home.

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:24.360
Quickly.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.010
Pay for it from my account.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.210
The PIN is my mother's birthday.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.450
And the second?

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.460
The second...

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:39.980
is to oust me from Ritzland Support Company.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.460
Oust you?

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.530
You're quitting?

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.530
But why? Where did that come from?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.220
What I'm about to do now is on my own terms.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.880
I want you to get rid of all my connections.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.960
I was just getting bored.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.000
Wanna have some fun?

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.850
I wouldn't mind waiting 
for you to free your hands.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.920
What's wrong?

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:48.500
Did I reopen an old wound?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.870
Your moves are so obvious.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:54.240
I'm trying to play fair, you know.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.630
Hey, what's going on here?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.250
Raise your hands and get on your knees.

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:03.380
Quit messing around, Nikka.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.360
What do you think you're doing?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.640
You can't even keep an eye on him?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.840
I'm just having some fun, man.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:12.520
Don't go ratting me out to Donny.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.650
Freaking spoiled brat.

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:17.400
Come on, don't bother.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.330
Forget it. We'll watch him.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.490
Go wag your tail at the boss or something.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:26.140
Hey, old man...

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.310
Lemme give you some advice.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.990
Always pay attention.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:37.980
See?

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.280
Told you.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.450
What was that?!

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.860
Get over here!

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.680
Contact the guards outside!

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.120
Huh.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.690
I actually don't mind being messy.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.240
Do we have trouble?

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.420
Yeah.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:15.190
That guest of ours is wreaking 
havoc in the residence.

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:18.290
Word is to keep the perimeter secure.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:22.960
Huh?

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.260
What is that car doing?

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:40.920
Shit!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:41.960
It's a dump truck!

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.650
It rammed right in!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.040
Intruder from the mountainside entrance!

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.360
Call for backup!

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.490
What the hell happened here?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:55.080
He did all this by himself?

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.980
Where's Nikka?

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.250
Don't know, don't care.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:02.720
Groups 1 and 2 are going to 
beef up the boss's detail.

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:04.640
Group 6 is to check outside.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.060
The rest of us will hold the exits 
so we don't have to chase him.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.630
Don't let him get away.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:41.010
That critical hit Hou landed still hurts.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.200
I even got hit by a ricochet because of it.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.340
What to do now...

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.340
You should have said something.

00:15:57.340 --> 00:16:00.310
At least introduce yourself.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:03.350
That would make things complicated.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.690
There's no point.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:10.550
Anyway, what do you plan to do now, Ryang-Ha?

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:16.860
Oh, dear...

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:20.790
What a terrible evening this has become.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.200
How sad.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:27.040
Truly sad.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:38.790
Whack!

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.650
Here we go.

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:49.360
Seriously?

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.360
It really was an old wound?

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.890
Who did this?

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:56.310
Huh?

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:13.590
What a lame way to die...

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.600
Come on, dude.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.950
Fine, then. Fine.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.700
Go ahead and die.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:36.110
I had high hopes for you, man.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.920
Oh, right. You hear that?

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:45.490
There's a hell of a commotion outside.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:51.650
Maybe we've got another guest.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.260
Check territory three 
via the property camera.

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:04.310
Don't miss them.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.590
Are you serious, Chateau?

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.900
This is beyond reckless.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:19.160
We don't even know if he 
gave us the right location.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.660
Mr. Song may not necessarily be there.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:26.150
Can't we at least wait to get 
more information out of him?

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:34.470
Well, not that you ever 
listen to what anyone says...

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:39.330
Chateau, it gets chilly in the evening.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.180
Here.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.470
I can't have you catching a cold.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.840
Looking after the staff's 
health is part of my job.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:51.130
I told you to oust me.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.190
I'm already...

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.690
I can't do that.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:56.210
Jim...

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:56.940
After all...

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.620
That would require various documentation,

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.950
reclamation of issued weapons 
and other equipment,

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:07.630
ammunition counts, usage reports, 
a farewell party, et cetera...

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.190
Heaps of clerical processing.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:13.960
Don't go thinking you're getting 
out of work that easily.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.060
So please...

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:20.450
Come back safely, please and damn you.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.360
And say hi to Mr. Song for me.

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:28.800
<i>We have a visual on camera.</i>

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:29.750
<i>One target.</i>

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:34.730
There's a high chance that 
Target 2 is Chateau Dankworth.

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:37.280
<i>You may fire, but don't kill her.</i>

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.130
Understood.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.120
Her loud entrance must have been a signal.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.390
They plan to rendezvous.

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:48.620
Hurry up and capture Ryang-Ha Song.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.620
Be especially careful around the exits.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.850
Report your current positions.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.630
Everyone better answer.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.880
First...

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.710
Nikka.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.740
You let Mr. Song go, didn't you?

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:28.400
What do you think you're doing?

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.660
Oh...

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:36.670
I don't like hunting corpses, that's all.

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.580
<i>Why?</i>

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:45.180
<i>You always pop up when I least want you to.</i>

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.930
<i>Why can't I find you when 
I'm looking for you?</i>

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.020
I'm driving her left.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.440
Someone get around her.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.690
Just don't shoot her.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.210
Got her!

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.250
Cease fire! Group 6, gather here!

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:19.360
Hey! I said you can stop shooting!

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.280
Just get over here and give me a hand!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.120
Hey.

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:43.190
That sure was foolish of you.

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:52.270
You're one to talk.

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:39.050
Next episode: "Help."
